# Contains Duplicate

## Pattern
Set

## Recognition
- Check if duplicates exist
- Return True if any duplicate is found
- Return False if all elements are unique

## Approach
- Create an empty set.
- Traverse the array.
- If the current element already exists in the set, return True.
- Otherwise, add the element to the set.
- If the loop completes, return False.

## Code

```python
def containsDuplicate(nums):

    seen = set()

    for num in nums:

        if num in seen:
            return True

        seen.add(num)

    return False
```

## Complexity

Time: O(n)

Space: O(n)

## Interview Tip

"I'll use a set because I only need to know whether an element has been seen before. Set lookup is O(1) on average, making the overall solution O(n)."

